Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:10.549 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  anyone  hello everyone with the mediums release  date fast approaching  we wanted to share with you nine curious  details about the game  that you probably never heard about  so let's take a deep breath and start  counting  number one the core idea of the medium  and of the two simultaneous worlds  started back in 2012.  the game was initially to be released on  wii u xbox 360  and the playstation 3. although it was  pretty much a different game back then  you can still find mentions of the  medium online  with the initial announcement in the  form of an actual postcard  still floating on the internet our times  have changed when it comes to marketing  games  number two two key characters of the  game marianne  and the nameless man that's bent on  revenge have been based on two famous  polish actors  veronica rosati who you will soon see in  never gonna snow again  help design marianne i need your help  first  while the man uses the likeness of  martin tarachinsky  [Music]  you can recognize as vasily borghoff  from the netflix original series  the queen's gambit number three  the medium is somewhat of a reunion tour  of the silent hill  dream team the game soundtrack is  co-created with sonnet hill's main  composer  akira yamaoka mary elizabeth makes her  return with vocals  [Music]  or troy baker plays the character of the  mall  why hide  silly little girl number four  the medium takes you to an abandoned  hotel called liva  although the name has been changed for  the game the place it actually does  exist  the real name is hotel krakovia and is  located in the city centre of krakow  poland the developers they wanted to  give it a one-to-one rendition  so they went and explored the place to  carefully recreate its atmosphere  you can take a look at it on google maps  in case you want to visit the place  before the game is released  [Music]  number 5 marion's home where the game  starts  is located in a real apartment building  in krakow poland  near mataka square curiously  the same building or rather what it  would be like in 2084  can also be found in blooper team's  previous release observer  system redux  number six all the cutscenes were mocked  and recorded by the lead developers  and meant as precise references for the  motion capture actors  these mock-ups proved invaluable when  the pandemic hit  and the proper recording sessions had to  be directed remotely  for the mocap sessions of the mall  bluebird team hired an actor  walking on stilts to better depict the  creature's towering posture  all in all the game has around 90  minutes of cutscenes  within an 8 to 10 hour long game with  some of the cutscenes using the dual  reality mechanic  so you can watch the events unfold from  two different perspectives  number seven you can check the level of  your spirit energy by looking at  marion's arm  this is just one of the ways that  developers wanted to make the game's ui  as minimal as they can so that the  players can immerse into the medium's  world  as much as possible number eight  the game takes place in an abandoned  communist resort so naturally  there are quite a few mentions and  objects in the game connected to that  era  including a wrecked mallow a cult  classic tiny polish car  now valued by fans of retro automobiles  worldwide  and finally number nine the medium hides  a lot of secrets pop culture references  and little easter eggs you can find  allusions to bloomberg team's previous  games  or for example spot some of the  developers on  postage stamps let us know what you  found once you get to play the game  happy hunting  [Music]  you

